{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Closing evidence (all 6 ACs met; landed as Gerrit change 2241, MERGED at LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1).\n\nAC1-AC2 (portable credential-free Cloud/DC E2E over the full taxonomy, no external credential / CI-provider trigger): tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_reconciler_coordinator.py (scenarios 1-6: mixed success + venue parity, transient recovery/fold, long-delay endpoint-fuse deferral, permanent-not-masked, provider-scope isolation, fuse open/reset) + test_reconciler_coordinator_taxonomy.py (7-10: label-first create/never-delete, restart observe-before-replay, commit_unknown partial, fail-open delivery). Credential-free verified-fake Cloud/DC via _coordinator_harness.py (frozen clock, no network). 47 passed.\nAC3 (route census + poison, no reachable removed fallback): test_coordinator_route_census.py green (route_for('create')=='coordinator'; legacy path poisoned).\nAC4 (ADR 0103 ownership/taxonomy/fuse/containment/deltas/cutover/no-delete rollback): finalized Proposed->Accepted with the failure-taxonomy (11->5 buckets), fuse/containment, and no-remote-delete rollback sections.\nAC5 (architecture/operator docs: versioned outcomes + future adapter obligations): docs/architecture.md RP-03 planner->coordinator->adapter section.\nAC6 (ADR numbering + doc index + architecture links): tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py + tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py green.\n\nTDD: behavioral tests authored held-out (a background agent authored the E2E suite from the venue-cutover wiring; edge/E2E withheld from it), validated independently, teeth-verified by mutation (replay_safety_for commit_unknown->safe made s8/s9 RED; removing the fuse is_fuse_eligible guard made s4 RED; both restored). No production code changed (validates merged S1-S4).\n\nCI note: ps1 hit a Verified-1 from an import-mode collision (engine-tier tests mislocated in the interface-parity tier poisoned sys.modules['rebar_reconciler'], breaking rebar_reconciler.classify.* collection). Fixed by relocating the suite to the unit engine tier (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/) next to the reused venue-cutover harness, removing the sys.path hack; ps2 passed both gates and merged. file_impact + verify_commands updated to the relocated paths."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787746400795401001,"uuid":"86bf048b-eceb-48f6-b74b-d8ac96cff6aa"}